{"id": "EUVD-2026-94306", "enisaUuid": "7c34275b-e592-3314-8f24-626d366d2c7b", "description": "GitAhead through 2.7.1 contains an OS command injection vulnerability in src/git/Filter.cpp that allows malicious repositories to execute commands by substituting crafted filenames into clean/smudge filter commands. Attackers can ship files named with $(command) selected via .gitattributes so checkout or staging runs the command through bash -c as the victim.", "datePublished": "2026-10-07T11:59:37", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-07T20:55:38", "baseScore": 7.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/gitahead/gitahead/issues/661", "https://github.com/gitahead/gitahead", "https://github.com/gitahead/gitahead/blob/v2.7.1/src/git/Filter.cpp#L43-L70", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/gitahead-through-2.7.1-os-command-injection-via-git-filter-filenames"], "aliases": ["GHSA-q252-mvpj-37m5", "CVE-2026-106058"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 1.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "b37df06b-44e4-3165-8a7f-22461f3ab0ad", "product": {"name": "GitAhead", "vendor": {"name": "gitahead"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.7.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0de7ef5c-5fef-3288-be3a-d6314b436a85", "vendor": {"name": "gitahead"}}], "isExploited": false}